WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:01.530
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.510
- [Narrator] This is the speech

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:04.590
that got China's most famous entrepreneur,

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.885
Jack Ma, into trouble.

00:00:05.885 --> 00:00:09.010
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.470
- He kind of slid directly into criticism

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.410
of the Chinese regulatory environment,

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.390
saying things, for example,

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.990
that China has a pawnshop mentality,

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.490
every traditional, old-school.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.430
But it didn't come off as very funny.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.347
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.520
(people cheering)

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.720
- [Narrator] Ma is the lead founder

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.860
of e-commerce giant Alibaba,

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.760
which is the FinTech giant
Ant Group grew out of.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.010
Both companies have
redefined China's economy.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.770
But Ma directly challenged the people

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.704
who oversee the country's
economy during this speech.

00:00:41.704 --> 00:00:44.760
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.730
- The speech really triggered
the central government,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.940
all the way up to President Xi Jinping.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.170
- [Narrator] So how did the
model of Chinese innovation

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.490
and entrepreneurial success end up facing

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.793
the ire of Beijing?

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.563
We look at three of his public
appearances to find out.

00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:04.830
(dramatic music)

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.130
- [Duncan] In the early
days, you knew Jack more

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.850
because of his humor and his charisma

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.430
than because for his company.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.910
- [Narrator] Duncan Clark first met Ma

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.370
when Alibaba was set up in 1999

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.910
as a fledging e-commerce company.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.770
The internet consultant based in Beijing

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.820
even wrote a book about this friend.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.653
- [Duncan] He had this sense

00:01:21.653 --> 00:01:23.703
that he was destined for great things.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.470
- [Narrator] Ma lived up
to his own expectations

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.923
as his startup grew
into a tech powerhouse.

00:01:32.098 --> 00:01:34.248
And he rubbed shoulders
with global elites.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.910
- Few people could be a better example

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.610
of the China dream.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:43.560
Jack Ma basically was the best PR

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.820
for the Chinese government.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.210
- We just press by.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.890
- [Lingling] He wants
to make a difference,

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:52.810
be it the advancement of
technology in China overall

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.530
or geopolitical matters.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.020
- [Narrator] As Ma
became the friendly face

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.720
of China's economic rise,

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.510
he found himself more
involved in politics.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.640
- Business and political leaders

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.660
would like to say that they knew Jack.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.000
When they visited China would,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.080
sometimes heads of state would
irritate the party actually

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.703
by making appointments for Jack.

00:02:15.144 --> 00:02:16.220
- [Narrator] One of the
most talked about encounters

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:17.710
was when Ma went to Trump Tower

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.230
to meet the president elect,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.890
less than two weeks
before the inauguration.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.210
- High-quality man.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.160
Thank you, Jack.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.240
- [Lingling] The foreign minister

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.040
was in dark about this meeting.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.310
They didn't know about it

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.480
until after the meeting
was all over the news.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.380
- And we also think that
China-US relationship

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.213
should be strengthened.

00:02:35.213 --> 00:02:39.110
- Some officials felt
like he should have stayed

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.570
in his own lane,

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.680
(bell ringing)
(people cheering)

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.600
which is being a businessman,

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.600
not crossing over to sensitive issues.

00:02:49.116 --> 00:02:51.100
- [Narrator] And this
wouldn't be the last time

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.423
Ma crossed the line.

00:02:54.519 --> 00:02:58.436
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.250
- [Narrator] Since 2013, Ma
had been slowly signaling

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.800
that he'd make his way out of Alibaba.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.320
- I can compete with the Bill
Gates who can retire earlier.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.810
- [Narrator] Then finally, in 2019,

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.050
he officially stepped
down as executive chairman

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:14.750
of the company at the age of 55.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:18.667
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.950
- [Lingling] It didn't
really come as a surprise

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.490
to a lot of officials

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:27.140
and some of them thought he's smart.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.286
He's basically wrapping up
a very successful career.

00:03:31.286 --> 00:03:34.760
♪ And sit while with me ♪

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.660
- [Narrator] But Ma's retirement

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.000
didn't mean he was going away

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.450
from the public eye.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.140
He pursued philanthropic causes

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.160
and became a judge on an
African reality television show,

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.900
similar to "Shark Tank."

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.060
- Let the competitors worry about you.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.590
- [Narrator] Ma also didn't fully leave

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.550
the tech world after retirement.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.930
He remained the controlling
shareholder of Ant,

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.600
which has changed the way
many people in China spend,

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.600
borrow, save and invest.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.130
The company has also worked with

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.120
and competed against state-owned banks

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.453
and other financial institutions in China.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.200
- His company Ant has
been acting like a bank

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.830
without being regulated as a bank.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.670
Ant has amassed a trove of consumer data.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:17.150
That data has allowed Ant Group

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.440
to stay many, many steps ahead

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.280
of traditional commercial lenders.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.040
- [Narrator] It was
very lucrative for Ant,

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.960
so much so that the company landed

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.300
in the crosshairs of Chinese regulators.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.450
- [Lingling] The central bank have wanted

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.200
to tighten the screw

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.178
over his companies for quite a long time.

00:04:36.178 --> 00:04:40.920
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.540
- [Lingling] But because
of his tremendous ability

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:48.440
to combine his entrepreneur ambitions

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.080
with his political savvy,

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:54.060
he have been able to basically fend off

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.770
that kind of pressure.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.040
- [Narrator] But the clash between Ma

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.340
and financial regulators
all came to a head

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.757
on October 24th last year.

00:05:01.757 --> 00:05:05.674
(speaking in foreign language)

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:10.828
- [Duncan] On this occasion in Shanghai,

00:05:10.828 --> 00:05:14.390
what he was saying was directly
criticizing actually people

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:16.510
in the room, which included
very senior figures

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.203
in the Chinese government
in financial regulation.

00:05:21.607 --> 00:05:25.524
(speaking in foreign language)

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.530
- The speech in Shanghai
was maybe a culmination

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.840
of where we'd gone from total
humility in the early days

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:37.620
to perhaps a touch of hubris.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.290
- [Narrator] Less than two
weeks after the speech,

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.680
Chinese regulators took action.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.980
- Ultimately, it was President Xi

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.740
who personally intervened in the matter,

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.800
called off the Ant IPO

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.380
and instructed financial regulators

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.520
to do a thorough investigation

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.750
into the risks posed
by Jack Ma's financial

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.760
and technology empire.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.240
- [Narrator] Ant has
said it's moving quickly

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.030
to try and address the
concerns of regulators.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.923
After the Shanghai speech,
Ma was nowhere to be seen.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:07.980
But three months later,

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.070
he reappeared in a video that was posted

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.360
to Chinese social media

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:15.230
by a government-backed news
outlet called Tianmu News.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:18.431
It showed him addressing
village teachers in China.

00:06:18.431 --> 00:06:22.060
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.347
- Senior officials don't want
to send the wrong message

00:06:24.347 --> 00:06:27.070
to the Chinese entrepreneurs,

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:32.000
okay, once you get big, this
is the consequence for you.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.470
The party leadership obviously want

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:38.690
to have very firm control over the economy

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:41.230
but another top priority

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:46.230
for the central leadership
is to keep innovation going.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.313
That's a very big challenge
for China going forward.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.040
- [Narrator] And Alibaba and
Ant are still a major part

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.640
of China's tech future

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:58.483
but it's an open question
what that means for Jack Ma.

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:03.050
- [Lingling] Is there a way
for him to redeem himself?

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.663
The jury's definitely still out.

00:07:05.663 --> 00:07:08.413
(dramatic music)

